{"id": "Dc9do-az5La", "title": "Video by coachkunaalnaik", "description": "Claude can feel brilliant at the start of a coding session.\n\nThen 40 prompts later:\n\nit forgets constraints.\nreopens solved problems.\ntouches unrelated files.\nand starts making weird assumptions.\n\nThe model didn’t suddenly get worse.\n\nThe context did.\n\nSo during longer builds, I periodically reset these 5 things:\n\n1. Current objective\n  What exactly are we solving right now?\n2. Decisions already made\n  Architecture, libraries and approaches we already agreed on.\n3. Files that matter\n  Stop carrying half the codebase forward when 4 files are relevant.\n4. Known constraints\n  What must NOT change?\n5. Definition of done\n  What evidence proves this task is actually complete?\n\nThen I give the agent one clean instruction:\n\n“Continue from this state. Don’t reconsider completed decisions unless new evidence requires it.”\n\nAI coding isn’t only about writing better prompts.\n\nIt’s about maintaining good context.\n\nAnd the longer your agent works, the more important that becomes.\n\nSave this before your next long Claude session.\n\nWant FREE Agentic Ai MASTERCLASS???\nCheck link in Bio!!", "channel": "coachkunaalnaik", "uploader_id": "1363056732", "uploader": "Kunaal", "timestamp": 1788869287, "like_count": 3, "comment_count": 12, "http_headers": {"User-Agent": "Mozilla/5.0 (Windows NT 10.0; Win64; x64) AppleWebKit/537.36 (KHTML, like Gecko) Chrome/149.0.0.0 Safari/537.36", "Accept": "text/html,application/xhtml+xml,application/xml;q=0.9,*/*;q=0.8", "Accept-Language": "en-us,en;q=0.5", "Sec-Fetch-Mode": "navigate", "Referer": "https://www.instagram.com/"}, "formats": [{"format_id": "dash-1072342368677676a", "ext": "m4a", "tbr": 81.773, "asr": 44100, "format_note": "DASH audio", "container": "m4a_dash", "vcodec": "none", "acodec": "mp4a.40.5", "url": "https://instagram.flis9-1.fna.fbcdn.net/o1/v/t2/f2/m78/AQNlaEXoKyTTGaEgwHhUL2wtgU94mfxHgtDGWerNRJgr6yufIyyd0zD5-Ifo1FvV0Hio